  "g_task_per_model": {
    "definition": "G_task(k) = sigma2_task / (sigma2_task + sigma2_residual/k), relative-error G for a task's score averaged over k occasions, computed SEPARATELY within each model via its own one-way random-effects ANOVA over tasks (task random, occasion residual) -- so sigma2_task and sigma2_residual here are model-specific, not the pooled two-way components above. This is an explicit choice: the task wording says 'computed within each model', which we read as a fully separate per-model one-way decomposition rather than reusing the pooled ANOVA components for every model (which would give identical G_task(k) across models).",
