      "definition": "Smallest k (occasions per task per model) at which the probability that the model with the lower true (observed) overall pass rate ('underdog') comes out ahead of the model with the higher true pass rate ('favorite') in a resampled comparison drops below 0.05. k=1 uses the exact closed-form value; k>1 uses the Monte Carlo table below. NOTE: this is biased downward -- the favorite/underdog label is read off the very same pooled sample that gets resampled, so a comparison against its own label can only look better than a comparison against an independent, freshly-drawn evaluation. See disagreement_probability for the unbiased two-independent-evaluations version.",
